  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n(14, 66, 19)\n\n(14 + 19) × 2 = 66\n\n33 × 2 = 66\n\n66 = 66 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n(43, 134, 24)\n\n(43 + 24) × 2 = 134\n\n67 × 2 = 134\n\n134 = 134 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo, checking each option one by one:\n\nOption 1) (45, 97, 4)\n\n(45 + 4) × 2 = 97\n\n49 × 2 = 97\n\n98 ≠ 97 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 2) (10, 35, 8)\n\n(10 + 8) × 2 = 35\n\n18 × 2 = 35\n\n36 ≠ 35 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 3) (6, 42, 15)\n\n(6 + 15) × 2 = 42\n\n21 × 2 = 42\n\n42 = 42 (LHS = RHS)\n\nOption 4) (37, 81, 4)\n\n(37 + 4) × 2 = 81\n\n41 × 2 = 81\n\n82 ≠ 81 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nHence, \"Option 3\" is the correct answer.",
